===Etymology 3===
From ''*čïn'' (“true, real”), presumably borrowed from Sinitic [[眞#Chinese|眞]] (''MC tsyin'', “true, real”).

Cognate with Old Uyghur <small>[script needed]</small> (čïn, “true, real”); Tatar [[чын#Tatar|чын]] (çın), Kazakh [[шын#Kazakh|шын]] (şyn), Uzbek ''[[chin#Uzbek|chin]]'', Khakas [[сын#Khakas|сын]] (sın), Tuvan [[шын#Tuvan|шын]] (şın, “true, real”), etc.

